<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Flight Centre lifts year net profit.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Flight Centre lifts year net profit.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    19.14 vs 7.57</p>
<p>    Net				     11.85 vs 4.79</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)	     4.50 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)	     8.00 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Sales				  968.80 vs 489.74</p>
<p>    Other income			   5.81 vs 1.80</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			   15.10 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Abnormal items		  loss 0.24 vs nil</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 percent franked  </p>
<p>Pay date October 15</p>
<p>Reg date September 30</p>
<p>    Tax					6.99 vs 2.59</p>
<p>    Interest				 2.47 vs 1.67</p>
<p>    Depreciation			   3.15 vs 1.52</p>
<p>    Minorities			     0.06 vs 0.19</p>
<p>NOTE: Flight Centre Ltd is a travel agent chain that listed in December 1995.  </p>
<p>The company said 1995 comparison figures in the preliminary final statement did not represent a true result for that year and that figures in the company's October 1995 prospectus should be used. These figures were:</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    19.14 vs 10.83</p>
<p>    Net				     11.85 vs 7.62</p>
<p>    Sales				  968.80 vs 759.00</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
